How we worked it out
────────────────────
  Market scenarios
    We simulated 500 possible paths for the markets, month by month, by
    replaying blocks of past monthly returns, about 12 months at a time, in a
    random order (a stationary block bootstrap). The past returns are the
    assets' monthly returns from Nov 1996 to Oct 2026.

  Strong, average and weak markets
    The average market is the middle scenario (the median). Only 1 scenario in
    10 does better than the strong market (the 90th percentile), and only 1 in
    10 does worse than the weak market (the 10th).

  Chance
    The share of scenarios in which every payment from November 2046 to October
    2066 is made in full.

  Status
    Room to spare when the chance is at least 90%; on track when it is at least
    the 85% you want; nearly on track when it is up to 15 points below it; off
    track below that.

  Today's money
    Returns are after inflation (2.5% a year), so every amount is in today's
    money: 4,000 in 2066 buys what 4,000 buys today. Taxes aren't included.

  How much room there is
    Each change is worked out on the same scenarios, one at a time: the largest
    change that still keeps an 85% chance.

  Runs out
    The month the money can no longer pay in full. In a weak market, that is the
    month by which 1 scenario in 10 has run out; in an average market, half
    have.

  What if markets do worse
    Lower returns: every scenario earns 1 percentage point a year less. A crash:
    the markets of the worst 12 months in the data for your mix (Dec 2007 to Nov
    2008) replace the same months of every scenario; other mixes are tested with
    the same months.

  Worst year and largest fall
    Worst year in 20: only 1 twelve-month stretch in 20 of the scenarios loses
    more. Largest fall: the typical largest fall from a peak over the plan's 40
    years, before any money is paid in or out. Volatility: of the mix's monthly
    returns in the history, a year, before inflation.

  What this can't tell you
    The scenarios only replay months that happened, so none has a month worse
    than the worst in the data. The chance is an estimate from past markets, not
    a promise.

  Repeatable
    Seed 0: the same plan gives the same report.

  Important   The projections in this report about the likelihood of investment
              outcomes are hypothetical in nature, do not reflect actual
              investment results and are not guarantees of future results.
              Results may vary with each use and over time: different data,
              assumptions or seeds give different figures, while the same inputs
              and seed give the same report.

  Not advice  This report is for illustration and information only. It is not
              investment, financial, tax or legal advice, and it is not a
              recommendation or an offer to buy or sell any security or to
              follow any strategy. The changes it shows illustrate what the
              figures would need; they are not suggestions to act. Before making
              financial decisions, consider your own circumstances and, where
              appropriate, seek advice from a qualified professional.

